# .easignore — what EAS Build uploads when it packages this repo.
#
# THE ONE THING TO KNOW BEFORE EDITING THIS FILE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# It REPLACES .gitignore. It does not add to it. From the EAS build-archive
# reference: "EAS CLI will produce the archive by copying all files starting
# from the root of the git repository with the exception of .git, node_modules,
# and all files matched by rules from .gitignore" — and "`.easignore` can only
# be located in the root of your git repository and, if it is present, none of
# the existing .gitignore files will be respected by EAS CLI."
#
# So the intuitive edit — a short file listing "the extra stuff we don't need" —
# makes the archive BIGGER, not smaller, and does something worse than that:
# .env.local and .env.staging.local stop being ignored and get uploaded to a
# build server with the Supabase SERVICE ROLE KEY inside them. Everything
# .gitignore excludes has to be restated here, verbatim and in the same order
# (order is load-bearing in gitignore syntax: a later `.env*` re-ignores what an
# earlier `!.env.example` un-ignored).
#
# That duplication is a drift hazard, and it is fenced rather than trusted:
# apps/mobile/src/release/release-config.test.ts asserts that every rule in
# .gitignore also appears here, so adding a secret to .gitignore and forgetting
# this file turns the mobile suite red instead of leaking on the next build.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS: the first real build (2026-08-26, 9900114a-c134-41cf-af38-
# 6aaf789d2942) reported "Your project archive is 152 MB". Measured against the
# tracked tree that day (exact bytes, `git ls-files` + `stat`): 126.3 MB, of
# which docs/ alone is 84.4 MB and dim-interno:docs/reviews 74.9 MB of that — screenshots,
# measurement dumps and a 12 MB zip of one critique's captures. Every build pays
# that upload, on a connection that is not a datacentre's.
#
# The three additions below take the tracked tree from 126.3 MB to 34.7 MB.
# THE 152 IS NOT RECONCILED WITH THE 126.3 and this comment will not pretend it
# is: eas-cli is not a dependency here, so the archive was never produced
# locally to be weighed. The honest number for the effect of this file is the
# next build's own "Your project archive is N MB" line.
#
# WHAT IS EXCLUDED BEYOND .gitignore, and why each one is safe: the three
# additions at the bottom are read by NO code that runs during a native build.
# That was swept rather than assumed — every reference to `docs/`, `__tests__/`
# and `e2e/` from app, apps, components, lib, src, db and packages is inside a
# comment.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* EXCLUDED. The web app's own source (app/,
# components/, lib/, src/, public/) stays. It is most of the 34.7 MB left and
# the Android build does not read it either — but `pnpm install` runs at the
# repo root against this workspace, packages/contract is a real dependency of
# apps/mobile (`@dim/contract: workspace:*`), and an archive missing pieces of
# the workspace fails in a way that looks like a dependency problem rather than
# an ignore rule. Three additions that take away 73% of the tracked tree is the
# whole win; the rest is not worth a build that fails for a reason nobody
# guesses.

# ===========================================================================
# Everything below, down to the ADDITIONS marker, mirrors .gitignore verbatim.
# Keep it in sync — the fence test will tell you if you don't.
# ===========================================================================

# dependencies
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# build outputs
.next/
out/
dist/

# Expo (apps/mobile)
.expo/

# environment
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
!.env.example
!.env.local.example

# editor
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# misc
.turbo/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# supabase local
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/
supabase/snippets/Untitled*.sql

# agent/script scratch output, and the root session scratch (build artifacts, QA state)
tmp/
/scratchpad/

# agent tool caches
.atl/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/hooks/

# design handoff reference
design_handoff_*/
install.cmd

# playwright
playwright-report/
test-results/
e2e/.auth/

# vercel CLI
.vercel/
.superpowers/

# local demo screen recordings
*.webm
scripts/assets/pet-photos-real/*
!scripts/assets/pet-photos-real/README.md
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
.design-sync/.cache/
.design-sync/learnings/
.design-sync/node_modules

.vercel
.env*

# Playwright MCP session artifacts, and playwright-cli's page snapshots
.playwright-mcp/
.playwright-cli/

# Graphify knowledge-graph output
graphify-out/

# Scratch scripts from parallel QA agents
scripts/scratch/
scripts/bulk-cursor-pets-staging.mjs

# Playwright MCP writes snapshots and screenshots to the repo root
/*.png
/*-snapshot.md
/panorama.md

# vitest --reporter=json output
.vitest-report.json

# Local Definition-of-Done gate evidence (one dir per run, at the repo root).
# Anchored: an unanchored `gate-*/` matches at any depth. Verbatim from
# .gitignore — release-config.test.ts compares the two rule for rule.
/gate-*/

# QA session-minting output — carries live session tokens
qa-sessions*.json

# playwright-cli's browser storage-state files — same reasoning as
# qa-sessions*.json above. Verbatim from .gitignore — release-config.test.ts
# compares the two rule for rule.
*.auth-state.json
*-auth-state.json
storage-state*.json
auth.json
my-session.json

# Firebase Admin SDK service-account keys — verbatim from .gitignore, and this
# copy matters MORE than that one. Keeping the key out of git keeps it off a
# public repo; keeping it out of here keeps it out of the archive uploaded to
# EAS on every build. A credential that never reaches GitHub but rides along in
# every build upload has not been protected, only moved.
#
# NOT google-services.json, which is committed on purpose and which the build
# actually needs — see the note beside these two lines in .gitignore.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
service-account*.json

# A ROOT app.json is Expo debris. The real one is apps/mobile/app.json.
/app.json

# ===========================================================================
# ADDITIONS — not in .gitignore. Tracked files a native build never opens.
# ===========================================================================

# 84.4 MB of the 126.3 MB tracked tree, almost all of it dim-interno:docs/reviews/results:
# screenshots, measurement dumps and a 12 MB zip of a critique's captures.
# Prose and images. Nothing under here is imported, required, or read at
# runtime by anything in the app.
docs/

# The web app's Vitest suite (6.7 MB). Runs on CI and on a developer's machine;
# a Gradle build has no idea it exists.
__tests__/

# The Playwright suite. `e2e/.auth/` is already excluded above as a secret;
# this excludes the specs themselves, which are equally irrelevant to a build.
e2e/

# The prebuild output, if a developer ever ran `expo prebuild` locally. It is
# ignored by apps/mobile/.gitignore rather than by the root .gitignore (that
# file's header explains why), and .easignore does not read nested .gitignores
# — so without these two lines a local prebuild would be uploaded and land on
# top of the one EAS runs for itself. Nothing here is tracked today; these are
# a fence against a directory that appears the first time somebody debugs a
# native build on their own machine.
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/ios/

# The five .claude/* mirror lines above (verbatim from .gitignore) re-include
# skills/, settings.json, agents/ and hooks/ for GIT TRACKING purposes — none
# of that is read by a native build. This bare rule sits AFTER those
# negations, so gitignore's "a later parent-directory exclusion wins"
# ordering takes the whole folder back out of the archive.
.claude/

# Restated from .gitignore (this file REPLACES it, it does not extend it).
# Generated by scripts/copy-maplibre-worker.ts for the WEB build; the mobile
# upload has no use for it and no reason to carry half a megabyte of it.
/public/maplibre/
